From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ep9
Subject: [PATCH] Add Limits: a step budget and an interrupt poll for a
 search

A backtracking search can take exponential time (/(a+)+b/ on a long
run of a's), and an embedder that must stop a script (a timeout, a
terminate request) has no way to end it: the search runs to its end.

Regex::find_limited searches a UTF-16 or UCS-2 text like
find_from_utf16 / find_from_ucs2, but counts steps: a start position,
a backtrack or a loop iteration (also each iteration of a loop whose
body matches one character: greedy, lazy or counted). Every
poll_interval steps it calls the caller's poll callback; true ends the
search with Stopped::Interrupted. An optional budget ends it with
Stopped::BudgetExceeded. A stop inside a lookaround stops the whole
search. Searches without limits count against a counter that never
runs out, so their results do not change.

Test: tests/limits.rs.
